===Etymology===
{{ryu-kanjitab|yomi=k|すら}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ryu|ja|空|tr=sora}} (or more exactly, an earlier form of it). 

As remarked by Igarashi (2022)<ref>Igarashi, Yosuke. "[https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/opli-2022-0193/html Reconstruction of Ryukyuan tone classes of Middle Japanese Class 2.4 and 2.5 nouns]".</ref>, the inherited meaning of this term in Ryukyuan languages is not "sky", but "treetop".

